  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "Fig. 2: Model architecture for spatial representation. Black arrows indicate excitatory pathways, while red arrows indi- cate inhibitory pathways. Positional input drives the grid cell network, compass input drives head direction cells, and lidar input drives boundary vector cells (BVCs). Grid cell and BVC signals provide afferent excitation to the place cell network, while afferent and recurrent inhibition regulate competition and sparsity. Head direction signals provide a shared orienta- tion reference between grid and boundary representations.",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
